@c CHAPTER: CLI
@node CLI
@chapter CLI

Guile Documentá comes with the @command{documenta} program, which
recognizes the following subcommands:

@quotation Note
Guile Documentá does not currently extract @abbr{CLI, Command Line
Interface} documentation from the source code, but it is intended to
do so in the future. The following documentation is (re)written by
hand (sadly).
@end quotation


@deffn Command extract source [destination]
Extract the documentation of the library defined in the @var{source}
path.

@defvr Argument source
A path to a Guile Scheme module file or to a directory
containing Guile Scheme modules. For example:
@code{"project-x/libx.scm"}, @code{"project-z/libz"}.
@end defvr

@defvr Argument destination
Optional path to a directory where the final
Texinfo files will be saved. If not provided, @var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH}
is used (see the module @ref{documenta-commands}).
@end defvr
@end deffn
