@node Development
@appendix Development

The development of this project happens in a private
@abbr{PMS, Project Management System}, but the source files are
publicly available in a
@url{https://codeberg.org/luis-felipe/guile-documenta, git repository}.

To start working on a new version of the software (say @samp{X.Y.Z}):

@enumerate
@item
Add the new version to the PMS.

@item
Define goals for the new version.

@item
Report to the issue tracker the work to be done to achieve those
goals.

@item
For each issue reported to the tracker:
@enumerate
@item
Make the necessary changes to the source files.

@item
Test the changes.

@item
Document the changes.

@item
Mention the changes in the version history if they are important
(@pxref{Version History}).
@end enumerate

@item
Release version @samp{X.Y.Z}:
@enumerate
@item
Update the release date of version @samp{X.Y.Z} in the version history
of the documentation (@pxref{Version History}).

@item
Update online manuals (for all supported languages).

@item
Update the project website (if any).

@item
Tag the latest revision as version @samp{X.Y.Z}.

@item
Announce the release to the world.
@end enumerate

@end enumerate


